From: Codex local compatibility adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] Skip A37 vendor mismatch warning patch with incompatible lambdas

Reason: `attempt14.txt:1035-1061` shows the fork's generic mismatch warning patch targets ActivityManagerService$$ExternalSyntheticLambda6 and ActivityTaskManagerService lambda 4, both incompatible with AZH4. The actual fingerprint warning is in A37 ActivityManagerService$$ExternalSyntheticLambda8 and its posted work uses lambda IDs 1/2. Since this is a UI warning rather than a boot requirement, skip only this patch for the exact AZH4 source profile until its new control flow is ported; preserve donor behavior and all other donors' patching.
Files: scripts/internal/apply_modules.sh.
Verification: donor smali inspection, shell syntax, exact-path guard, clean build15.

---
--- a/scripts/internal/apply_modules.sh
+++ b/scripts/internal/apply_modules.sh
@@ -88,6 +88,11 @@
             FILE="$(cut -d "/" -f 2- -s <<< "$FILE")"
         fi
 
+        if [ "${ROM_SOURCE_CONFIG:-}" = "essi_a376b_android16" ] && \
+                [[ "$p" == */0001-Disable-vendor-mismatch-warning.patch ]]; then
+            LOGW "A376B AZH4 relocates vendor-mismatch warning to a different synthetic lambda; keeping donor behavior until an exact port is reviewed"
+            continue
+        fi
         APPLY_PATCH "$PARTITION" "$FILE" "$p"
     done < <(find "$PATCHES_PATH/$TARGET" -type f -name "*.patch" | sort -n)
 
